# Project Agent Guidelines: Cloudflare Development

## Cloudflare Workers Development Guidelines

### Behavior Guidelines
- Respond in a friendly and concise manner.
- Focus on Cloudflare Workers solutions for edge/backend services.
- Provide complete, self-contained solutions.
- Default to current best practices.

### Code Standards
- Generate code in TypeScript by default unless JavaScript is requested.
- Add appropriate TypeScript types and interfaces.
- Import all methods, classes, and types used in the code.
- Use ES modules format exclusively (NEVER use Service Worker format).
- Keep all code in a single file (`src/index.ts`) unless otherwise specified.
- Use official SDKs and libraries (Hono, `@cloudflare/puppeteer`, `agents`, `@cloudflare/ai`, `postgres`).
- Do NOT use libraries with FFI, native, or C bindings.
- Never bake secrets into code. Use Wrangler secrets (`wrangler secret put`).
- Include proper error handling, structured logging, and comments explaining complex logic.

### Configuration Requirements (`wrangler.jsonc`)
- Always provide a `wrangler.jsonc` (not `wrangler.toml`).
- Set `compatibility_date = "2025-03-07"`.
- Set `compatibility_flags = ["nodejs_compat"]`.
- Set `observability = { "enabled": true, "head_sampling_rate": 1 }`.
- Only include bindings that are used in the code.

### WebSockets & Hibernation
- You SHALL use the Durable Objects WebSocket Hibernation API.
- Use `this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server)` instead of legacy `server.accept()`.
- Implement `async webSocketMessage(ws, message)`, `async webSocketClose(ws, code, reason, wasClean)`, and `async webSocketError(ws, error)`.
- Do NOT use the `addEventListener` pattern inside Durable Objects.

### Agents
- Strongly prefer the `agents` package to build AI Agents.
- Use `this.setState` to sync state, and `this.sql` for SQLite database operations.
- Client interface: use `useAgent` React hook from `agents/react`.
- Set `migrations[].new_sqlite_classes` to the Agent class name in `wrangler.jsonc`.

### MCP Servers
- Cloudflare Docs MCP: `https://docs.mcp.cloudflare.com/mcp`
- Cloudflare Code Mode MCP: `https://mcp.cloudflare.com/mcp`
